WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.684
Start with three scores.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.905
Exponentiate each one.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.957
Add them up: the denominator.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.389
Divide each by the sum: half, quarter, quarter.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.718
Real scores can be negative; their exponentials cannot.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.105
Divide by the sum: weights.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.351
All positive, and totalling one.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.345
Raise score three by one.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.009
Its weight grows; every other shrinks, because the total stays one.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.144
Divide each score by a temperature, tau. Hot levels the weights.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.531
Cold sharpens them: token five takes most of the weight.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.935
Without root d, sixty-four dimensions mean tau of one eighth.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.365
The output is the values' weighted average.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.899
Hot, it sits near the plain mean.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.625
Cold, it reaches value five, still inside.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.124
A plain sum counts everyone equally: eight times the mean.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.295
It lands outside the values.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.711
Softmax weights compete for a total of one, and the output is a weighted average of the values.
